# What Vercel must not upload. Deliberately short.
#
# The project root for this deployment is the REPO root, not `edu-site`, and
# that is not a preference — it is required. `edu-site/scripts/check-references.mjs`
# resolves `REPO` to `path.resolve(cwd, "..")` and then stats repo-root paths
# (CLAUDE.md, PROJECT-MAP.md, stack.md, history/reports/*, .claude/skills/*,
# curriculum-state, edu-site/README.md). Upload only `edu-site` and those eleven
# stats fail, the gate reports them as `scan-root-missing`, and the build exits 1.
# Verified by running the gate against a simulated `edu-site`-only tree.
#
# So: do not add anything here that a referenced document might name. Every path
# below was grepped for first and appears in no scanned file. Anything excluded
# that a doc DOES name becomes a dead-reference failure on the next deploy.

# 818 MB, reinstalled by the installCommand.
edu-site/node_modules

# Regenerated by buildCommand. Excluded on purpose: if the build ever fails, a
# stale build/ that had been uploaded could otherwise be served as a successful
# deploy. Leaving it out makes a failed build fail visibly.
edu-site/build
edu-site/.docusaurus

# Local dev-server logs and one-off scripts.
edu-site/.local-logs

# Vercel reads the working copy, never the git history.
.git
